 {"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M23443Z65RK83WTF4Z7D7PGD","node":"reviewer","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-09T13:04:35Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"The seed brief (fabro-eb3f) said the revisor fallback 'actually lives in analyze.md step 1 (line 48)' and warned not to transcribe 'Step 3.5' — but the revisor file's section is genuinely headed 'Step 3.5' with the fallback at item 1/line 48, so brief and seed named the same location differently and the warning was a false divergence. Implementer summary then described the 'real location' as 'analyze.md Step 3.5', compounding the confusion. Fix idea: when a brief corrects a seed's path citation, quote the actual heading text from the target file so the implementer and reviewer don't have to re-litigate which identifier is right."}],"observations":["Verified the churn-only loop diff against the per-seed claim base (f5eea5a) independently via git; evidence capture matched the repo exactly (planner.md +1/-1, issues.jsonl +1/-1, clean worktree).","Read the revisor analyze.md to confirm the Step 3.5 cross-reference resolves to a real section containing the journal fallback — the citation is accurate despite the brief's contradictory path-correction note.","Capability check: prompt-only change, no credential/tool surface changes; the edit consumes no engine-provided capability (local journal read via shell only)."]}}
