 {"id":"fabro-f5d7","title":"Engine: persist a read-only run/automation state snapshot reachable from the run workspace","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T12:33:28.569Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T12:42:40.863Z","description":"Run 01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1's implementer journal (stage implementer@1, seed fabro-91ff) reports the runs/automation DB state from runs 01M22X67GYXC/01M22VF9PWJH is not reachable from the product repo, so an incident-citing seed forced a superset fix whose regression test asserts guard semantics rather than the incident path — and the alternative cause (open fabro-ee5d) may remain unfixed. Change: engine-side (fabro-store / fabro_runs_list), persist per run a read-only fabro ps -a --json-style state dump, or extend the run projection with a status timeline, that the implementer can read. Complementary to fabro-5a25 (stage records into worktree) and fabro-313c (repo-snapshot context key) — different target (runs/automation state vs stage records/repo snapshot), cross-referenced not superseded. Effect: incident-citing seeds become verifiable and fixes target the actual cause instead of the union of hypotheses. Basis: run 01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1, workflow version fdcab06ec2d4960a3fe766ddfcda5b5639105f463e9e6cb414f4c8e48485976f, commit 11017eb56dd3a2bc74357d3f7cc3a0bbcf13cdcf","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-6997","title":"Develop planner prompt: two footgun one-liners — fs_hide glob returns empty, never rg -rn","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T12:33:43.081Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T12:42:40.781Z","description":"Run 01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1's planner globbed .fabro/workflows/develop/** under fs_hide and got a silently empty result (events seq 46-47), then burned a shell ls/rg round to locate prompts (seq 52-54); that same call ran rg -rn \"fabro_runs_list\" .fabro -l — harmless only because -l discards -r replacements. The existing fs_hide note in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 3 covers read_file denial only. Add two one-liners to planner.md: (a) glob on fs_hide paths returns EMPTY, not an error — go straight to shell for .fabro/**; (b) never rg -rn, -r replaces — use -n. This extends open fabro-2eb6's implementer-side rg discipline to the planner (different file, complementary); engine-side glob notice is open fabro-8296. Effect: −2 tool calls and −1 LLM round per planner pass touching platform paths. Basis: run 01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1, workflow version fdcab06ec2d4960a3fe766ddfcda5b5639105f463e9e6cb414f4c8e48485976f, commit 11017eb56dd3a2bc74357d3f7cc3a0bbcf13cdcf","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-154c","title":"Develop reviewer prompt: state whether a seed-spec mandate satisfies ADR-0019","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T12:33:55.205Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T12:42:40.684Z","description":"Run 01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1's reviewer (observation 2) had to adjudicate whether revisor Step 3.5's git fetch origin <base-branch> — a new code path on the engine credential bridge, mandated by the seed spec — counts as a recorded user decision under ADR-0019, and ratified it as spec-mandated by judgment call. Add one line to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md pinning the rule (a seed-spec mandate is or is not a recorded user decision for capability-delta verdicts). Effect: identical capability-delta verdicts across reviewers instead of adjudications that can flip between false blocks and silent ratification. Basis: run 01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1, workflow version fdcab06ec2d4960a3fe766ddfcda5b5639105f463e9e6cb414f4c8e48485976f, commit 11017eb56dd3a2bc74357d3f7cc3a0bbcf13cdcf","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
